(Two Stages of Photosynthesis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Light-dependent reactions:) Tj
T*
(   - Take place in the thylakoid membranes.) Tj
T*
(   - Water is split \(photolysis\), releasing oxygen as a by-product.) Tj
T*
(   - Produce ATP and NADPH.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Light-independent reactions \(the Calvin cycle\):) Tj
T*
(   - Take place in the stroma of the chloroplast.) Tj
T*
(   - Use ATP and NADPH to fix carbon dioxide into glucose.) Tj
T*
(   - This stage does not directly require light.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Factors that affect the rate of photosynthesis include light) Tj
T*
(intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, and temperature.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
